# behavior: private helpers that only read a Rust tree value walk it from a field, from a parameter, through a helper chain and through a cursor without copying the tree (the crate's clone counter stays at 0); an explicit clone counts once; a child taken as an owned value counts its subtree; a snapshot taken before the owner is replaced counts the whole tree; a tree handed to functions declared over a reference, to a returned callable, to a trait default's callable, to a returned cursor, to a helper that clears it and to a walk over a reference parameter adds nothing; and a helper handed the same tree twice costs one copy of it
